{% set local_problem %}
<p>Decatur's location along the Tennessee River creates drainage challenges that many homeowners don't fully appreciate until water damage appears. The river's influence raises local water tables, meaning the ground is often already saturated when storms hit. Add Morgan County's red clay soil — which doesn't absorb water well — and you have a recipe for foundation problems.</p>

<p>Many older Decatur homes, especially in the historic Bank Street and Albany areas, still have original sectional gutters that are decades past their prime. These homes were built when gutter technology was simpler and less effective. The seams in traditional gutters are failing, leaking behind the fascia, and directing water toward foundations rather than away from them.</p>

<p>Even newer Decatur construction often has inadequate gutters. Builder-grade sectional systems are chosen for cost, not performance. With Decatur receiving 55+ inches of rain annually, these budget gutters quickly show their limitations — overflowing during storms and developing leaks at every seam.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters solve these problems at the source. No seams means no leak points. Custom fabrication means gutters sized correctly for your roof's water volume. The result is reliable drainage that protects your home from Decatur's unique combination of river proximity, high water tables, and heavy rainfall.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are exactly what they sound like: continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. Unlike traditional sectional gutters (which are made of pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together), seamless gutters are fabricated on-site from a single piece of aluminum coil — custom-cut to the exact length of each run on your home.</p>

<p>Why does this matter? Because seams are where gutters fail. Every joint in a sectional gutter system is a potential leak point, a place for debris to catch, and a weak spot that can separate over time. In Decatur's climate — with heavy rains, humidity, and temperature swings — these seams deteriorate faster than in milder regions.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Decatur home, feed in aluminum coil, and fabricate your gutters right in your driveway. What comes out is a precision-fit gutter system designed specifically for your roofline — not generic sections forced to fit.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>Blue River Gutters is headquartered just 25 minutes away in Huntsville, and we've been serving Decatur and Morgan County for over 20 years. We're not a national franchise — we're your neighbors who understand the specific challenges Decatur homes face.</p>

<p>We know the Tennessee River's impact on local drainage. We've worked on historic homes throughout downtown Decatur and understand the architectural considerations. And we can be on-site quickly if a storm causes damage. That's the advantage of working with a truly local company.</p>
